Make the plain-algebra walk name-aware. Replace `isPlainJoinAlgebra(extension.getArg())` with `isPlainJoinAlgebra(extension.getArg(), assignmentNames)` where the Filter case becomes:

```java
if (tupleExpr instanceof Filter filterArg && !filterArg.isVariableScopeChange()) {
    if (filterArg.getCondition() instanceof SubQueryValueOperator) return false;
    Set<String> conditionNames = VarNameCollector.process(filterArg.getCondition()); // descends into EXISTS bodies (AbstractSimpleQueryModelVisitor visits subqueries)
    conditionNames.retainAll(pushedNames);
    if (!filterArg.getArg().getAssuredBindingNames().containsAll(conditionNames)) return false; // pushed var only possibly bound below this filter -> boundness observable
    return isPlainJoinAlgebra(filterArg.getArg(), pushedNames);
}
```
StatementPattern, non-scoped BindingSetAssignment and non-scoped Join cases are unchanged (bound evaluation of an SP/BSA with x=v equals unbound evaluation filtered by compatibility, and Join distributes). Keep the existing possible-name containsAll at :133 as a cheap precondition (it only blocks). Implement the predicate as `BindingScopeAnalysis.filterDependsOnlyOnAssured(Filter, Set<String>)` in the shared helper (see sharedInfrastructure) so LMDB rewrites can reuse it. Sound because: for each pushed name n mentioned by a Filter f, n ∈ assured(f.arg) means every row reaching f already carries n, join compatibility forces it to equal the VALUES value, so f evaluates identically in bound and unbound form; names not mentioned by f cannot change f's outcome; BIND expressions were already required not to mention n.

Add one predicate and use it at the three sites. In FilterRelocator (or in shared BindingScopeAnalysis and call from here):

```java
/** Filter may move into `target`, one operand of a binary operator whose other operand is `sibling`. */
private boolean canPushInto(TupleExpr target, TupleExpr sibling) {
    if (!target.getBindingNames().containsAll(filterVars)) return false;      // existing precondition (possible names may only block)
    Set<String> assured = target.getAssuredBindingNames();
    Set<String> siblingPossible = sibling.getBindingNames();
    for (String v : filterVars) {
        if (!assured.contains(v) && siblingPossible.contains(v)) return false; // sibling could supply v after the join
    }
    return true;
}
```
meet(Join): `if (canPushInto(left, right)) {…existing left branch…} else if (canPushInto(right, left)) {…} else relocate(filter, join);`
meet(LeftJoin): `if (canPushInto(leftJoin.getLeftArg(), leftJoin.getRightArg())) leftJoin.getLeftArg().visit(this); else relocate(filter, leftJoin);`
meet(Extension): additionally require `Collections.disjoint(filterVars, elementNames)` (an Extension element that rewrites a filter variable makes the pushed filter observe the pre-BIND value).
Soundness: the filter's outcome depends only on filterVars; for each v, either target assures v (merged value == target row value by compatibility) or the sibling can never bind v (merged value == target row value, possibly unbound in both). Union/Intersection cloning and Difference→left remain exact. shouldKeepFilterAtJoin cost logic is untouched (it only decides between the two already-sound positions).

