Flip to the declared contract (denylist) and drop the CodeSource dependence:

```java
private static Effect functionEffect(String iri, Effect arguments) {
    Function function = FunctionRegistry.getInstance().get(iri).orElse(null);
    if (function == null) return Effect.UNKNOWN;               // unresolvable: cannot evaluate anyway, fail closed
    if (function.mustReturnDifferentResult()) return Effect.VOLATILE;
    if (arguments == Effect.VOLATILE || arguments == Effect.UNKNOWN) return arguments;
    if (function instanceof Now) return Effect.QUERY_STABLE;   // shared per query, not repeatable across queries (LMDB FilterSurfaceKey needs this distinction)
    return arguments;                                          // REPEATABLE, or QUERY_STABLE inherited from a NOW() argument
}
```
